WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.002
A moving average is different from a running total because the calculation uses a limited number of nearby rows.

00:00:08.002 --> 00:00:13.502
Suppose daily sales are ten, twenty, thirty, and forty.

00:00:13.502 --> 00:00:20.137
A three-row moving average for the fourth row uses twenty, thirty, and forty.

00:00:20.137 --> 00:00:23.638
The earliest value has moved outside the frame.

00:00:24.088 --> 00:00:30.571
This kind of calculation smooths short-term variation while still following the sequence over time.
